  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "F5yCxyZrMdB2HKIfrXe9Nxi4UKM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:12.735Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The named categories are system integrators, ERP and similar integrators, management consultancy, and AI change management.\n\nChoosing the consultancy as the buyer follows from the industry criteria: if an industry is network-shaped and already buys consultancy, then the consultancies are the concentration point in an otherwise dispersed market. One integration plus one partner conversation can reach many end clients, which is the only way a small vendor covers a long tail.\n\nIt also sets the terms of the pitch. A consultancy buys what makes its own offering more sellable, so the argument has to be about their proposition rather than about the technology's merits.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:12.735802Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:12.735807Z"
    }
  },
